# CBflow — code ownership routing
#
# PR reviews auto-request from the discipline that owns the touched path.
# Edits to global/ require integrator sign-off (shared tooling blast radius).
#
# Patterns use GitHub's CODEOWNERS syntax. Rightmost pattern wins when
# multiple patterns match — list specific patterns AFTER general ones.

# Catch-all — integrators review anything that doesn't match a specific rule.
*                     @cbflow-integrators

# Shared infrastructure — integrator sign-off required.
/global/              @cbflow-integrators
/bin/                 @cbflow-integrators
/.github/             @cbflow-integrators

# Discipline-owned trees.
/PD/                  @pd-team
/DFT/                 @dft-team
/DV/                  @dv-team

# Shipped user-facing docs (edits need review from docs or discipline leads).
/docs/                @cbflow-integrators @pd-team

# Operator-facing scratch (not shipped — anyone can touch).
/workarea/
/inputs/
/test_releases/
